<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Goiota - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/goiota/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/goiota/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 20250528</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_20250528/</link><pubDate>Wed, 28 May 2025 12:23:23 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_20250528/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import (&#10;&#9;&amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;)&#10;&#10;type Direction int&#10;&#10;const (&#10;&#9;North Direction = iota&#10;&#9;East&#10;&#9;South&#10;&#9;West&#10;)&#10;&#10;func (d Direction) String() string {&#10;&#9;return [...]string{&amp;#34;North&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;East&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;South&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;West&amp;#34;}[d]&#10;}&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10;&#9;fmt.Println(South)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Reference answer and explanation: &amp;ldquo;South&amp;rdquo;. Key takeaways: usage of iota, and a type&amp;rsquo;s String() method.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Based on the usage of &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt;, the value of &lt;code&gt;South&lt;/code&gt; is inferred to be 2. Additionally, if a type defines a &lt;code&gt;String()&lt;/code&gt; method, &lt;code&gt;fmt.Printf()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fmt.Print()&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;fmt.Println()&lt;/code&gt; will automatically use the &lt;code&gt;String()&lt;/code&gt; method to print the string representation.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 175</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_175/</link><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jan 2025 10:15:27 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_175/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;&#10;const (&#10; a = iota&#10; b = iota&#10;)&#10;const (&#10; name = &amp;#34;name&amp;#34;&#10; c = iota&#10; d = iota&#10;)&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; fmt.Println(a)&#10; fmt.Println(b)&#10; fmt.Println(c)&#10; fmt.Println(d)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;0&#10;1&#10;1&#10;2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/3owhzDo5QeG" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 class="heading-element" id="first-const-block"&gt;&lt;span&gt;First &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#first-const-block" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;a = iota&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; starts counting from &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; in a &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block, so &lt;code&gt;a = 0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;b = iota&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; increments to &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;b = 1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 class="heading-element" id="second-const-block"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Second &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#second-const-block" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;name = &amp;quot;name&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is not used, but &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rsquo;s initial value is &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;, and it increments to &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt; after declaration.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;c = iota&lt;/code&gt;: The current &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; value is &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;c = 1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;d = iota&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; continues to increment to &lt;code&gt;2&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;d = 2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 class="heading-element" id="key-rules"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Key Rules&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#key-rules" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; starts counting from &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; in each &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Each line of constant declaration (whether &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is used or not) increments &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; by &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; in different &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; blocks are independent of each other.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 093</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_093/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:21 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_093/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;type Direction int&#10;&#10;const (&#10; North Direction = iota&#10; East&#10; South&#10; West&#10;)&#10;&#10;func (d Direction) String() string {&#10; return [...]string{&amp;#34;North&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;East&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;South&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;West&amp;#34;}[d]&#10;}&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; fmt.Println(South)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Reference answer and explanation: &amp;ldquo;South&amp;rdquo;. Key takeaways: usage of iota, and a type&amp;rsquo;s String() method.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Based on the usage of &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt;, the value of &lt;code&gt;South&lt;/code&gt; is inferred to be 2. Additionally, if a type defines a &lt;code&gt;String()&lt;/code&gt; method, &lt;code&gt;fmt.Printf()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fmt.Print()&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;fmt.Println()&lt;/code&gt; will automatically use the &lt;code&gt;String()&lt;/code&gt; method to print the string representation.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 091</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_091/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:18 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_091/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;const (&#10; a = iota&#10; b = iota&#10;)&#10;const (&#10; name = &amp;#34;name&amp;#34;&#10; c = iota&#10; d = iota&#10;)&#10;func main() {&#10; fmt.Println(a)&#10; fmt.Println(b)&#10; fmt.Println(c)&#10; fmt.Println(d)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Reference Answer and Analysis: 0 1 1 2.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Key takeaway: Usage of iota.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is Go language&amp;rsquo;s constant counter, and can only be used in constant expressions.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is reset to 0 when the &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; keyword appears, and each new line of constant declaration in a &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block increments &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; by one.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 028</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_028/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 19:49:55 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_028/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile? If so, what will be the output?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;const (&#10; x = iota&#10; _&#10; y&#10; z = &amp;#34;zz&amp;#34;&#10; k &#10; p = iota&#10;)&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; fmt.Println(x,y,z,k,p)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Reference Answer: Compiles and outputs: 0 2 zz zz 5&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When defining &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt;, if a variable is not followed by a value, it will use the value of the previous variable.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;const (&#10; x = iota&#10; _ = iota&#10; y = iota&#10; z = &amp;#34;zz&amp;#34;&#10; k = &amp;#34;zz&amp;#34;&#10; p = iota&#10;)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is equivalent to the line index of the &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>